{"step_index":260,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-31T19:19:47Z","content":"# AutoMind AI — Homepage Hero Section Built\n\nThe full-screen cinematic **Homepage Hero Section** for **AutoMind AI** is built in [`frontend/components/home/hero-section.tsx`](file:///C:/Users/chauh/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/automind-ai/frontend/components/home/hero-section.tsx) and live in [`frontend/app/page.tsx`](file:///C:/Users/chauh/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/automind-ai/frontend/app/page.tsx).\n\n---\n\n### Highlights of the Implementation\n\n#### 1. Cinematic Visual Hierarchy & Typography\n* **Main Headline**:\n  ```text\n  THE FUTURE OF\n  MOBILITY\n  ```\n  Rendered with high-contrast gradient chrome and cyan glow drop-shadow.\n* **Supporting Text**: `\"AI-powered intelligence for the way you drive.\"`\n* **Telemetry Eyebrow**: `LiveBadge` with pulsing status beacon for `\"Next-Gen Automotive Platform\"`.\n\n#### 2. Dual Action CTAs\n* **Primary CTA**: `\"Explore Cars\"` (cyan glowing button with spring hover physics, linking to `/explore`).\n* **Secondary CTA**: `\"AI Car Finder\"` (frosted glass button with pulsing cyan sparkle icon, linking to `/ai-finder`).\n\n#### 3. Central Vehicle Visual & Atmospheric Lighting\n* **Atmospheric Depth**: Top radial cyan spotlight cone, ground reflection light plate, and ambient backlight pulse.\n* **Aerodynamic Vehicle Silhouette**: Precision chassis curves, canopy glass reflections, carbon wheels, matrix laser headlights (cyan glow), and OLED tail lamp (crimson glow).\n* **Floating Physics**: Framer Motion hover/breathing float (`y: [0, -8, 0]`, 5.5s loop).\n* **Telemetry Overlays**:\n  * Left HUD Card: `0-60 MPH // 2.8s (Launch Control)`\n  * Right HUD Card: `PEAK POWERTRAIN // 750 HP • Dual-Motor AWD`\n  * Bottom Spec Ribbon: `Active Torque Vectoring`, `800V Architecture`, `380 mi EPA`, `AI Confidence: 98.4%`.\n\n#### 4. Animations & Micro-Interactions\n* **Entrance Choreography**: Staggered slide-up and fade-in transitions using custom cubic-bezier curves (`[0.16, 1, 0.3, 1]`).\n* **Scroll Indicator**: Bottom center animated scroll mouse indicator with smooth scroll trigger.\n* **Fully Responsive**: Scales cleanly across mobile viewports, tablets, and desktop displays.\n\n---\n\n### Verification\n* **TypeScript Typecheck (`npx tsc --noEmit`)**: **0 errors**\n* **Next.js Production Build (`npm run build`)**: **Compiled successfully with all static pages optimized**\n\nDetails are updated in the [Walkthrough Artifact](file:///C:/Users/chauh/.gemini/antigravity/brain/10f22c6a-7cf9-4af6-ab9e-ed172ecaddf1/walkthrough.md)."}
{"step_index":261,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-31T19:21:02Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nNow move to STEP 6: create the automotive data architecture for AutoMind AI.\r\n\r\nThe homepage hero is already implemented and verified successfully. Do not modify the existing hero section unless absolutely necessary.\r\n\r\nGoal:\r\nCreate a clean, scalable vehicle data layer that will later support:\r\n\r\n* car exploration\r\n* search\r\n* filtering\r\n* car details\r\n* comparison\r\n* AI recommendations\r\n* ML price prediction\r\n* Gemini AI assistant\r\n\r\nCreate a TypeScript vehicle model/type containing:\r\n\r\n* id\r\n* brand\r\n* model\r\n* variant\r\n* year\r\n* price\r\n* currency\r\n* fuelType\r\n* transmission\r\n* bodyType\r\n* horsepower\r\n* torque\r\n* mileage\r\n* engine\r\n* seating\r\n* safetyRating\r\n* bootSpace\r\n* dimensions\r\n* features\r\n* image\r\n* gallery\r\n* description\r\n\r\nCreate realistic development seed data with at least 20 vehicles across multiple brands and body types.\r\n\r\nInclude a mixture of:\r\n\r\n* hatchbacks\r\n* sedans\r\n* SUVs\r\n* luxury cars\r\n* electric vehicles\r\n* performance cars\r\n\r\nImportant:\r\n\r\n1. Keep vehicle data separate from React components.\r\n2. Create reusable TypeScript types.\r\n3. Create a clean service/repository layer for accessing vehicle data.\r\n4. Add functions for:\r\n\r\n   * getAllCars()\r\n   * getCarById()\r\n   * searchCars()\r\n   * filterCars()\r\n   * sortCars()\r\n5. Keep the architecture ready to replace the seed data with PostgreSQL/Supabase later.\r\n6. Do not put database logic inside UI components.\r\n7. Do not hard-code individual vehicle objects inside pages.\r\n8. Do not implement Gemini yet.\r\n9. Do not implement ML yet.\r\n10. Do not create the 3D viewer yet.\r\n11. Do not unnecessarily modify the existing homepage.\r\n\r\nUse proper TypeScript types and clean separation of concerns.\r\n\r\nAfter implementation:\r\n\r\n* run TypeScript checking\r\n* run the production build\r\n* fix any errors\r\n* tell me exactly which files were created/modified\r\n* tell me how the vehicle data architecture works\r\n\r\nDo not proceed to the next feature after this.\r\n\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-09-01T00:51:02+05:30.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
